From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] Marshal only the descriptor pointers a write's type uses

A descriptor write's pointers that its type does not use are ignored, and
DXVK points all three of them at one union of descriptor data. Without the
ignored-handles stream feature the encoder marshals every pointer that is
not null: for a uniform buffer bound at an offset it read the offset as an
image view and faulted inside vkUpdateDescriptorSets. Under Wine the fault
abandons the call with the encoder lock held, and every thread that calls
into the driver afterwards spins on it. The unused pointers are now
cleared before the write is marshalled
(caboose-features/d3d11_emulation.h).
---
 src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
index 64f1c2b..7acf44a 100644
--- a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
+++ b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
@@ -6278,6 +6278,10 @@ void ResourceTracker::on_vkUpdateDescriptorSets(void* context, VkDevice device,
 
     memcpy(transformedWrites.data(), pDescriptorWrites,
            sizeof(VkWriteDescriptorSet) * descriptorWriteCount);
+    // The marshaller follows every pointer that is not null, also those a write's type does
+    // not use (caboose-features/d3d11_emulation.h).
+    for (VkWriteDescriptorSet& write : transformedWrites)
+        caboose::features::clearIgnoredDescriptorPointers(write);
 
     size_t imageInfosNeeded = 0;
     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < descriptorWriteCount; ++i) {
-- 
